cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ARANDU TAPE in your research, please cite the archived software version."
title: "ARANDU TAPE: Adaptive Desktop Environment"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Werlang
    given-names: Rafhael Brum
repository-code: "https://github.com/werlangunipampa-web/ARANDU-TAPE"
abstract: "Experimental Linux desktop environment exploring spatial organization, accessible human-computer interaction, and design heuristics inspired by meaningful learning. Its public components include Seed and River navigation, GNOME and GTK interfaces, and an optional window-operation laboratory. Automated contract and build tests do not establish real-world usability or learning outcomes."
keywords:
  - Linux
  - GNOME
  - human-computer interaction
  - accessibility
  - meaningful learning
  - adaptive interfaces
  - spatial interaction
